  "recipes": {
   "css": "<h1 class=\"glitch\" data-text=\"ERROR\">ERROR</h1>\n.glitch { position: relative; color: #fff; }\n.glitch::before, .glitch::after {\n  content: attr(data-text); position: absolute; inset: 0;\n  background: var(--bg); /* 원래 글자를 밴드 부분만 가림 */\n}\n.glitch::before { left: -2px; text-shadow: 5px 0 cyan;\n  animation: band 2s infinite linear alternate-reverse; }\n.glitch::after  { left: 2px;  text-shadow: -5px 0 red;\n  animation: band 3s infinite linear alternate-reverse; }\n@keyframes band {\n  0%   { clip-path: inset(20% 0 50% 0); }\n  20%  { clip-path: inset(60% 0 12% 0); }\n  40%  { clip-path: inset(43% 0 40% 0); }\n  60%  { clip-path: inset(8% 0 78% 0); }\n  80%  { clip-path: inset(70% 0 6% 0); }\n  100% { clip-path: inset(32% 0 55% 0); }\n}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .glitch::before, .glitch::after { animation: none; display: none; } }",
   "canvas": "// 몇 프레임만 띠를 잘라 어긋나게\nfunction draw(ctx, t) {\n  const f = Math.floor(t * 12), on = hash(f) > .7;\n  ctx.fillText(text, x, y);\n  if (!on) return;\n  for (const [col, dir] of [['red', -1], ['cyan', 1]]) {\n    const y0 = top + hash(f + dir) * h * .8, bh = h * (.06 + hash(f * 3 + dir) * .2);\n    ctx.save(); ctx.beginPath(); ctx.rect(0, y0, W, bh); ctx.clip();\n    ctx.clearRect(0, y0, W, bh);\n    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'screen';\n    ctx.fillStyle = col; ctx.fillText(text, x + dir * 6, y);\n    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#fff'; ctx.fillText(text, x + dir * 2, y);\n    ctx.restore();\n  }\n}",
   "ae": "1. 텍스트 레이어를 3개 복제하고 이펙트 「채널 시프트」로 R만 / G+B만 남긴다\n2. 그리기 모드를 스크린으로 해 겹친다\n3. 위치 X에 식: posterizeTime(12); random() > .85 ? value + [random(-12,12),0] : value\n4. 「베네치안 블라인드」 또는 사각 마스크로 가로 밴드만 어긋나게(2~4프레임)",
   "aeEn": "1. Duplicate the text layer ×3; use Shift Channels to keep R only / G+B only\n2. Set blending to Screen\n3. Position X expression: posterizeTime(12); random() > .85 ? value + [random(-12,12),0] : value\n4. Use Venetian Blinds or rectangle masks so only horizontal bands shift (2–4 frames)"
  },
